BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261013T060000
DURATION:PT45M
SUMMARY:onlyspx 6am pivots and premarket posts: completed on rerun
UID:26b7e2a7-b4bd-4e11-adfc-634c503cd0f1@26b7.org
DESCRIPTION:The scheduled 6am pivots run walled at a sign-in step-up in 
 the\ncodespace browser session\; a manual rerun shortly after loaded\nwith
  no challenge and produced the day's pivot\, volatility\, and\nrange 
 values. The composed premarket post in the locked format\nwas published 
 and verified live as text on the three text\nchannels and as an image on 
 the photo and video channels\,\ncompleting the full premarket set. A retry
  ladder for session\nwalls was built into the job.
DTSTAMP:20261015T063033Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261013T063700
DURATION:PT45M
SUMMARY:Exit-interview system built on GitHub
UID:47a9e036-bf09-4fcb-a450-d84597093140@47a9.org
DESCRIPTION:A standing rule was established that every piece of agent 
 work\,\nscheduled or interactive\, ends with a structured exit 
 interview\ncovering steps taken\, retries\, access\, the user's concerns\,
  and\nresolution. A dedicated GitHub repository was created as 
 the\ncanonical store\, the first reports were written and pushed\, and\na 
 read-before rule was wired in so each recurring run reads the\nprevious 
 run's interview first. The steps-taken section was\nadded the same morning
  and the day's earlier reports were\nbackfilled to match.
DTSTAMP:20261015T063033Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=/ics.py/2020.1/America/Toronto:20261013T063000
DURATION:PT30M
SUMMARY:MapleScholar morning investigation: Analytics day
UID:5a469aee-7a7d-4638-b95b-8e0cc67417a0@5a46.org
DESCRIPTION:Read-only investigation completed. Analytics showed 
 conversions\nscaling across several firing key events\, with a top 
 paper\nholding its lead. Flags: a not-found page appearing among the\ntop 
 pages\, a share of users with no country recorded\, and a\nsmall 
 unassigned-traffic segment. Ads email and in-product\nchecks showed no new
  policy gaps\; a long-standing Search\nConsole validation item remains 
 pending. Nothing was applied\nanywhere.
DTSTAMP:20261015T063033Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
